{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794511098,"nonce":"3vP0IG8SQoUJKEn5vjgTpRqeg+Q=","title":"wasm direct: a function the AIR pipeline refuses is not stubbed under --allow-refused","message":"`--allow-refused` turns a function the direct emitter cannot emit into a body that raises through hlp_error, so its callers still link. A function that fails earlier, in `air_pipeline::optimized`, is dropped by `wasm_direct::emit_into` without being reported or stubbed: it is neither in `emitted.functions` nor in `emitted.skipped`. Callers then import `Fun_\u003cn\u003e` and the link fails on an undefined symbol, or with a function that was never defined.\n\nFix: report it in `skipped` with the pipeline's error, and give it the same stub. The stub has to be declared before the callers are emitted (an import and a definition of one name are two symbols in the object builder), so either pre-declare from a first pass over `optimized`, or let ObjectBuilder turn an import into a definition in place.\n\nNo program is known to hit this; the repo's test programs and Pocket Studio are all fully direct. A test needs a body the pipeline refuses.","files":null}]}